    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** lineup for August 26th is headlined by the powerhouse trio of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (74.34), **Gunnar Henderson** (79.38), and **Kyle Tucker** (78.13). **Gunnar Henderson** holds our highest efficiency score of the day, buoyed by a favorable matchup against the right-handed McGreevy and a robust +14% dynamic platoon boost. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** is positioned to feast against Smith-Shawver; the opposing xERA of 5.23 provides the runway for **Kyle Tucker** to maximize his ceiling in a high-leverage scoring environment. **Jackson Merrill** also remains a core start (75.26), benefiting from an elite matchup against Chandler that mitigates minor park-factor concerns.\n\nOur most complex decision centered on the bottom of the order, specifically evaluating **Nasim Nunez** (54.10) versus the volatility of **Luis Robert Jr.** (45.13). While **Luis Robert Jr.** possesses elite raw tools, his score is currently depressed by a significant negative platoon adjustment and a restrictive matchup against May, which limits his base-stealing potential. Conversely, **Nasim Nunez** earns the nod in the UTIL spot due to a favorable SB environment; his ability to exploit the slow delivery of Gordon gives him a higher floor in our scarcest category. **Liam Hicks** (54.11) occupies the C1 spot, maintaining his value through a strong platoon advantage against the right-handed Melton. \n\nWe are monitoring the status of several bench assets, specifically **Heliot Ramos**, who remains our primary backup option should a late-lineup change occur. Our depth is currently hindered by the IL stints of **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson**, forcing us to rely on the current active configuration to maintain game caps. We are also keeping tabs on our depth prospects like **Sam Antonacci**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, and **Tommy White**, who remain on standby should we need to adjust for defensive flexibility or late-breaking weather patterns. Be advised that **Luis Robert Jr.** carries the highest risk profile tonight; should his start become jeopardized by defensive rotation, we will pivot to maintain our speed-first strategy.",
